From 1d09574cedb420afb3cb67e61d7ea85165e83730 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yaegerbomb42 <yaeger.james42@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 11:50:16 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat(usage): usage & cost meter with
 per-run/per-day/per-provider aggregation
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds a usage and cost meter for t24:
- lib/telemetry/usage.ts: pure aggregation projection over the durable runtime
  ledger (tasks + runs) into all-time totals, per-run rows, per-day buckets and
  per-provider buckets.
- app/api/runtime/usage/route.ts: scoped GET returning { usage }.
- minimalist-ui UsageMeter component rendered in the Telemetry panel (all-time +
  today totals, top providers), polling every 30s with graceful degradation.
- tests/usage.mjs: isolated-home aggregation tests (totals, ordering, day buckets,
  provider buckets, empty/missing-ledger states) — all pass via tsx.
- app/api/upload/route.ts: fix pre-existing broken @/middleware import (isLocal)
  to @/lib/auth isAllowed so tsc is green.

Verified: npx tsc --noEmit clean; next build succeeds; usage test passes.
